# The settings window (M8) — its own folder, because it is its own window.
#
# ⚠️ Registered here for the same reason as everywhere else: quickshell loads
# through a virtual filesystem, where QML's implicit "types in my own folder"
# rule does not apply. Without an entry the type does not exist, and QML says so
# by drawing nothing. See ../common/qmldir.
#
# SettingRow and SettingGroup live here rather than in common/ because nothing
# outside this window has settings rows in it. Toggle and TextField DO live in
# common/, because they are controls rather than rows and the shell already had
# five hand-drawn text fields for want of one.
SettingsWindow 1.0 SettingsWindow.qml
SettingsContent 1.0 SettingsContent.qml
SettingsRail 1.0 SettingsRail.qml
SettingGroup 1.0 SettingGroup.qml
SettingRow 1.0 SettingRow.qml
# The two settings that cannot be a row, each for a structural reason and each
# named in the exemption list of tests/setting-rows.sh: `outputs` is one object
# per monitor, `binds` is sixty-three of them.
OutputScales 1.0 OutputScales.qml
BindsList 1.0 BindsList.qml
